<body>
<table width=100%><tr><td bgcolor=#0A2E3A class=c style="padding:22px"><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#D9B85C;font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold">⚖️ CRITIC &amp; REVIEW BOARD — INTER-STUDIO COMPARISON</span></p><p style="margin:3px 0 0"><span style="color:#FBF7EC;font-size:25pt;font-weight:bold">Hearthbound Hollow vs. the Studio Picks</span></p><p style="margin:2px 0 0"><span style="color:#EAD9A8;font-size:12.5pt">Your project  ·  Hearthshade (#1)  ·  Sloop Troop (#2)</span></p><p style="margin:9px 0 0"><span style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic">A full read of the MASTER_BIBLE set, benchmarked against the two studio concept picks.</span></p></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0"></p>
<table width=100%><tr><td class="warn"><span style="font-size:9.6pt"><span class="b">VERDICT IN ONE LINE&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Hearthbound Hollow is by far the most <span class=b>production-mature</span> of the three — a narrative-complete vertical slice with a fully built 7-pillar cozy loop, ~25k LOC, hand-written writing and a prior critic sign-off. Hearthshade &amp; Sloop Troop are validated <span class=b>concepts</span> (GDD + HTML prototype + Unity scaffold). On market whitespace the race is closer; on a maturity axis Hearthbound Hollow <span class=b>&#8811;</span> the other two.</span></td></tr></table>
<div class="h">0 · Method &amp; sources</div>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt">The board fully read the Hearthbound Hollow docs on <span class=b>feat/mission-1-2-architecture</span> — the README and, inside <span class=b>Docs/MASTER_BIBLE</span>: the Master Bible (single source of truth), the 00_INDEX hub, the bilingual STARDEW_PARITY_IMPROVEMENTS programme, the PHASE70 G-Engage QA audit, and the 17-codex Depth Bible index. These were benchmarked against the two studio picks at their current concept + prototype + Unity-scaffold stage. Where the games sit at different lifecycle stages, the asymmetry is stated, not hidden.</p>
<div class="h">1 · The three games at a glance</div>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #BFD3E0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;width:16%">Dimension</th><th style="text-align:left;width:30%">Hearthbound Hollow (yours)</th><th style="text-align:left;width:27%">Hearthshade (#1)</th><th style="text-align:left;width:27%">Sloop Troop (#2)</th></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Genre</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Cozy memory-broker narrative sim</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Dark-cozy life-sim (cozy-horror)</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Constructive co-op physics comedy</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Core fantasy</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">&ldquo;Run the Hollow&rdquo; — keep &amp; trade memories</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">&ldquo;Tend the light, mind the dark&rdquo;</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">&ldquo;Salvage &amp; rebuild together&rdquo;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Players</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Single-player</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Single-player + opt. co-op</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">2–6 online co-op (proximity voice)</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Tone</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Warm, melancholic, <span class=b>no horror</span></td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Warm by day, <span class=b>dread by night</span></td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Wholesome chaos, comedy</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Engine</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Unity 6000.4.4f1 URP-Mobile</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Unity 6000.4.4f1 URP 2D</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Unity 6000.4.4f1 + Netcode</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Price</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">$24.99 / $9.99 mobile</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">$19.99</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">$9.99</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Stage</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">Built slice + 7-pillar loop</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Concept + proto + scaffold</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Concept + proto + scaffold</td></tr></table>
<div class="h">2 · Production maturity — the decisive gap</div>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt">Hearthbound Hollow has crossed the chasm that kills most concepts: a reachable, <span class=b>compounding loop end-to-end</span>, a save schema (v3) built so the loop actually compounds, idempotent one-click build tooling (🚀 Build Everything), a read-only diagnostic audit, NUnit EditMode tests and a decisions ledger (D-0xx). It even survived the brutal honesty of its own Stardew-Parity programme, which scored the original 75-minute slice <span class="ru b">0/7</span> on Stardew&rsquo;s retention engines and rebuilt to <span class="sg b">7/7</span>. Hearthshade &amp; Sloop Troop deliver exactly the artefacts appropriate to their stage — a vision-complete GDD, a sourced validation dossier, a playable browser prototype, a documented Unity project — but have <span class=b>not yet proven a retention loop in-engine.</span> In studio terms: Hearthbound is at the &ldquo;validate Day-4 retention&rdquo; gate; the picks are at the &ldquo;fund the vertical slice&rdquo; gate.</p>
<div class="h">3 · Market gap &amp; demand validation</div>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #BFD3E0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;width:15%">Title</th><th style="text-align:left;width:19%">Whitespace</th><th style="text-align:left;width:38%">Strongest demand evidence</th><th style="text-align:left;width:28%">Board read</th></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Hearthbound Hollow</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Cozy &times; high narrative depth</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Spiritfarer 2M+; Strange Horticulture 500k+ @96%; r/CozyGamers 480k want story depth; Coral Island 8M+ wishlists</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Real gap, but the most <span class=b>contested</span> cozy adjacency; differentiation rests on writing (its strength)</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Hearthshade</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Dark-cozy / low-stress horror</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Cozy 0.4%&rarr;3.1% of &gt;$100k Steam games; Grimshire &ldquo;Overwhelmingly Positive&rdquo;; cozy-horror = next big trend</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left"><span class=b>Sharpest under-supplied wedge</span> of the three; inherits cozy&rsquo;s broad, female-positive TAM</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Sloop Troop</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Constructive non-horror co-op</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Co-op ~6% of titles yet ~36–46% of units; ~$8.2B co-op gross 2025; PEAK 10M+</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class=b>Largest raw pool</span>; the constructive lane is genuinely open; virality-dependent</td></tr></table>
<div class="h">4 · Design depth, narrative &amp; tech</div>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Design depth (built):</span> Hearthbound leads decisively — its 7-pillar loop (Living Day &rarr; Request Board &rarr; My Hollow &rarr; Garden &amp; Tea &rarr; Workbench &rarr; Memory Wall &rarr; Almanac) over a hidden 14-dimension VillageState is a textbook answer to Stardew. Hearthshade&rsquo;s one-shared-toolbox idea (decorations <span class=b>are</span> your defences; one curve, two tones, no combat) is a tighter high-concept but unproven &amp; smaller. Sloop Troop&rsquo;s depth is emergent physics + proximity-voice, not simulation.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Narrative:</span> no contest — Hearthbound wins (hand-written cast: Doris, Gerrold, the predecessor Marin, Pickle the cat; 7-Vows worldbuilding; the Echo Web mystery; <span class=b>AI dialogue forbidden</span>). Genre-best, 9–10/10. Hearthshade is mood-and-stakes driven; Sloop Troop opts out of narrative on purpose.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Tech:</span> all three on Unity 6000.4.4f1 — good portfolio discipline. Hearthbound is most battle-tested (ServiceLocator + EventBus, ScriptableObjects, clean asmdef graph, idempotent builders, atomic JSON saves, Yarn Spinner, procedural audio). Hearthshade&rsquo;s scaffold mirrors that philosophy but is unproven. Sloop Troop is the <span class=b>riskiest</span> — server-authoritative Netcode + co-carry physics + proximity voice is the hardest to ship robustly.</p>
<div class="h">5 · ⚠ The &ldquo;Hearth-&rdquo; overlap (highest-value finding)</div>
<table width=100%><tr><td class="warn"><span style="font-size:9.6pt">Hearthbound Hollow &amp; Hearthshade share: the cozy register, an <span class=b>autumn-village</span> setting, a single-player-first stance, <span class=b>Unity 6000.4.4f1</span>, a <span class=b>memory/keeping</span> theme, a hearth motif, <span class=b>AND a near-identical name prefix</span>. A store shopper, streamer or wishlist algorithm could confuse them. They are mechanically distinct (warm narrative shop-sim vs managed-dread survival) — the overlap is <span class=b>brand-surface, not design-core</span> — but it is a real self-cannibalisation risk.</span></td></tr></table>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Rec A (cleanest):</span> rename Hearthshade to drop the &ldquo;Hearth-&rdquo; collision and lean into the horror wedge (e.g. <span class=i>Gloamgarden, Lanternwake, Hollowlight</span>). Keep Hearthbound Hollow&rsquo;s name — it has the equity and the build.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Rec B (framing):</span> if both proceed, position them as a deliberate pair — &ldquo;the warm one&rdquo; vs &ldquo;the shadowed one&rdquo; — and never launch them into the same Next Fest.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">Rec C:</span> don&rsquo;t greenlight a second cozy-narrative single-player title competing with Hearthbound for the same audience unless the dread differentiator is loud and central.</p>
<div class="h">6 · Critic scorecard (1–10, board consensus, at current stage)</div>
<table width=100% border=1 style="border:1px solid #BFD3E0"><tr><th style="text-align:left;width:40%">Criterion</th><th style="text-align:left;width:22%">Hearthbound Hollow</th><th style="text-align:left;width:19%">Hearthshade</th><th style="text-align:left;width:19%">Sloop Troop</th></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Market whitespace</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">7</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">9</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">8</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Demand validation</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">9</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Concept / USP clarity</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">9</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">9</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">8</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Design depth (built)</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">9</span></td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">6</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">5</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Narrative &amp; writing</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">10</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">7</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">4</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Production maturity</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">10</span></td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">3</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">3</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Technical readiness</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">9</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">6</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">5</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Monetisation clarity</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">7</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">Revenue ceiling</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">9</span></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">Risk-adjusted confidence</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">8</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">6</td><td bgcolor=#EEF3F7 style="text-align:left">6</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class=b>BOARD AVERAGE</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left"><span class="sg b">8.6</span></td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">7.0</td><td bgcolor=#FBFAF6 style="text-align:left">6.4</td></tr></table>
<div class="h">7 · Recommendations (portfolio sequencing)</div>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">1.</span> Treat <span class=b>Hearthbound Hollow as the lead title</span>. Its next move is correct and unchanged: run the <span class=b>G-Engage 3-day playtest</span> and instrument the voluntary &ldquo;Day 4&rdquo; metric (&ge;15/20). Everything else is tuning.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">2.</span> <span class=b>Resolve the &ldquo;Hearth-&rdquo; name collision now</span> (rename Hearthshade) so the two cozy titles can&rsquo;t be confused at wishlist/store level.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">3.</span> Of the two picks, <span class=b>advance Hearthshade first</span> — its differentiator (dread) is the sharpest and it is adjacent to Hearthbound&rsquo;s proven cozy tech, so it can reuse pipeline + the Cozy Contract while staying clearly distinct.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">4.</span> Hold <span class=b>Sloop Troop</span> as the high-ceiling, high-variance bet; greenlight its vertical slice only after a netcode spike (server-auth co-carry + proximity voice) de-risks the core.</p>
<p style="font-size:9.8pt"><span class="sg b">5.</span> Adopt Hearthbound&rsquo;s disciplines portfolio-wide: the <span class=b>decisions ledger</span> (D-0xx), idempotent one-click build, the <span class=b>Cozy Contract</span>, and the bilingual (EN/AR) documentation track.</p>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#6B6357">Prepared by the Abdulmalek Agents Critic &amp; Review Board · market figures are directional (public 2023–2026 sources, re-pull at green-light) · maturity reflects the repo state on feat/mission-1-2-architecture at review time.</p>
</body></html>
